# Regression pin — dead-store elision vs emission-nop divergence
# (audio v2 chantier, 2026-07-19). `info->a = mirror[id].a` with `info`
# a far pointer param: the loaded value's spill was elided because an
# intervening `extuw Kl` (pointer low-half materialisation — REAL code)
# was nop-listed by mark_dead_stores' scanner. The consumer (storew's
# r1-in-A-cache path) then read the never-written slot: garbage stores.
# Fix: is_nop_instruction mirrors every emission-side skip condition
# (leaf_opt gate + cls != Kl on extensions).
#
# The pin: every far load feeding a far store must spill before A is
# clobbered — i.e., an indirect load is IMMEDIATELY followed by a store
# of its result. Two field copies in getinfo -> at least 2 such pairs.

# Re-pinned 2026-07-22 (issue #132): the invariant is "an indirect load
# is IMMEDIATELY followed by a spill of its result", not one particular
# spelling of the spill. With the load-forwarding word-size fix the
# emitter uses `pha` for one of the two copies and `sta N,s` for the
# other; both preserve the value, and pinning only `sta` made a
# correctness-neutral codegen improvement look like a regression.
in getinfo: absent lda\.l \$0000,x\n\tlda
count 2 lda\.l \$0000,x\n\t(?:sta|pha)
